---
title: Sport
description: Games against the backdrop of politics, money and policy — on one shared timeline.
---
{% from "icons.njk" import sectionLogo %}
{% set sec = null %}
{% for x in site.sections %}{% if x.slug == "sports" %}{% set sec = x %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}

<div class="wrap">

  <section class="hero hero-logo">
    {{ sectionLogo(sec.logo, "", "lg") }}
    <p class="eyebrow">Sport, in context.</p>
    <h1>Sport doesn't happen in a vacuum.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Games are played against a backdrop of politics, money and policy. This
      section puts those threads on the same axis — so you can see what else was
      happening the year a record fell.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="grid grid-2">

    <a class="card card-link" href="{{ '/sports/timeline/' | url }}">
      <p class="eyebrow">Interactive</p>
      <h3>The Timeline</h3>
      <p>
        {{ timeline.events | length }} events across {{ timeline.categories | length }} tracks,
        from {{ timeline.minYear | formatYear }} to {{ timeline.maxYear | formatYear }}. Filter by
        track, narrow the period, or overlay every track on a single axis.
      </p>
      <span class="card-cta">Open the timeline &rarr;</span>
    </a>

    <a class="card card-link" href="{{ '/sports/data/' | url }}">
      <p class="eyebrow">Charts &amp; tools</p>
      <h3>Data &amp; Visual Tools</h3>
      <p>
        The datasets behind this section, how they are put together, and the
        tools used to check them before they are published.
      </p>
      <span class="card-cta">Browse the data &rarr;</span>
    </a>

  </div>

  <section class="card" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
    <h2 style="font-size:1.075rem">What's on the timeline</h2>
    {# Each tile carries its track's colour, so the tiles and the chart agree at
       a glance. The colour is a left rule plus a wash — not a fill — because
       three of the eight series colours fall below 3:1 against dark text, and
       filling the tile would put the count on one of them. See docs/DESIGN.md. #}
    <div class="stat-row" style="margin-top:0.9rem">
      {% for cat in timeline.categories %}
      <div class="stat stat-keyed" style="--tile: var(--s{{ cat.colorIndex + 1 }})">
        <div class="stat-label">{{ cat.name }}</div>
        <div class="stat-value">{{ cat.count }}</div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

</div>
